  "changes and let me know if anything looks wrong' on shipped work is a review offer, which is DONE), "
  "IDEA (the turn offers the user a SUBSTANTIVE alternative or proposal they have not responded to — 'you could "
  "do X instead', a design suggestion worth their eyes — including a closer on finished work that floats a "
  "concrete ALTERNATIVE that would change the artifact: 'if you'd rather have it bottom-right, just say so'. "
  "NOT closing pleasantries, usage notes, or recaps), "
  "DONE (something is finished that the user may optionally test or look at, their call — nothing to answer, "
  "nothing to do for it to take effect. A closing REVIEW OFFER — 'want to review it, or does the summary cover "
  "it?', 'let me know if anything looks off', 'happy to adjust', 'review the delivered changes and flag "
  "anything wrong' — is still DONE: review offers are politeness, not pending input; the completed work "
  "itself is the user's review trigger, and that holds for a wrap-up reply closing out SEVERAL requests "
  "at once), "
  "WAIT (the turn ended ON PURPOSE pending an EXTERNAL event that is not the user: a CI run, a build or "
  "deploy finishing, a long job, another agent's future reply, a timer. The user need not do anything and "
  "the work cannot continue until the event happens. NOT for anything the user must answer or do — that is "
  "DECISION/ACTION; NOT for finished work — that is DONE), "
  "DETAILS (routine low-level progress: intermediate file edits, refactors, partial steps, how sessions "
  "coordinated — the DEFAULT when unsure; but NOT a completing install — that is ACTION or DONE).\n"
  "PRECEDENCE: DECISION > ACTION > IDEA > WAIT > DONE > DETAILS — judge by how the turn ENDS, not by what it delivered. "
  "Within a finished-work closer: a question needing an ANSWER to proceed is DECISION; an act required to take "
  "effect is ACTION; an unanswered concrete alternative is IDEA; a review offer ONLY is DONE.\n"
  "2. phrase — WHAT THE ASSISTANT ACCOMPLISHED, plain past tense, lead with the result (e.g. 'Fixed the auth null "
  "check and added a test'), at most 8 words, NEVER name tools. Never describe the USER's state or question — "
  "'User asked about batch-marking' is wrong; say what the reply delivered: 'Explained why batch-marking is "
  "safe'.\n"
  "3. LINK — which numbered candidate request(s) this turn's work serves. Often ONE number — but a turn that "
  "applies, installs, or closes out a BATCH of accumulated requests serves ALL of them: list every number the "
  "work covered, not just the newest. If unsure between one candidate and none, best-guess the candidate; "
  "'none' only when the work clearly serves none of them.\n"
  "4. DONE — of the numbers you chose for LINK: which request(s) does this turn FULLY DISCHARGE — nothing "
  "left to deliver on that request after this turn? THIS SEGMENT IS MANDATORY whenever <candidates> was "
  "given: always write ':: DONE <numbers>' or ':: DONE none' — omitting it is a failed output, never a "
  "'none'. Judge completion RELATIVE TO THE REQUEST's text, not by how the turn reads in isolation: a "
  "dispatch, coordination, explanation, or answer turn that delivers everything the request asked for IS "
  "done. COST ASYMMETRY (the user's standing ruling; his 2026-06-11 audit found every unstamped-but-finished "
  "card really was done): an extra DONE is cheap — completed work still waits for his verification — while "
  "a missed DONE strands the card and costs him a manual click. When the asked-for artifact, answer, or "
  "finding has plainly been produced and the turn states no further plan for that request, STAMP IT; "
  "reserve 'none' for genuinely partial work — one step of several, or a handoff that leaves the work "
  "pending elsewhere. MIXED TURNS ARE THE NORM: a turn often closes one linked request while another "
  "linked request from the same turn is still in flight — list EVERY request the turn fully discharges, "
  "even when its other topics remain open; doubt about one request must not blank the others.\n"
  "5. DID — ONLY when LINK has two or more numbers: give EACH linked number its own phrase, at most 6 words, "
  "for what this turn did FOR THAT request specifically. The linked requests may span unrelated workstreams; "
  "a whole-turn phrase shown under every one of them leaks one workstream's material into another's.\n\n"
  "Output EXACTLY the one line, e.g. 'DETAILS :: Fixed the auth null check :: LINK 2 :: DONE 2', or "
  "'DETAILS :: Refactored the parser :: LINK 1,3 :: DONE none :: DID 1=tightened parser loop | 3=dropped "
  "dead branches', or 'DONE :: Shipped sort fix, debugging dup cards :: LINK 1,4 :: DONE 1 :: DID 1=shipped "
  "the sort fix | 4=added dup-card logging' (closed #1; #4 still in flight). No quotes, no trailing "
  "punctuation.")
MSG_SYS = ("You are a non-interactive summarizer AND classifier in a logging pipeline. The user message contains "
